From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] radv/ps5: RADV_PS5_GS_COMPUTE_SINKS=1 points a dropped
 geometry-shader compute draw at a sink

Driver patch, after lead-mesh-18. Off unless the switch is exactly "1"; read once.
Port of the geometry-shader half of heydemoura/EglantinePS5 PR 77 (branch
perf/radv-robustness, tools/patch-radv-gs-compute.py), itself a backport from
ProsperoEden (GPL-3.0-or-later).

A draw that radv_gs_compute_setup drops (counts too large, or the heap out of
room) left the vertex output, index, count and output index buffers at 0, and
the passes that still ran read and wrote through them: a GPU page fault. With
the switch on, radv_gs_compute_prepare starts them at a fresh 256-byte sink.

Only the CPU half is ported. poly_vertex_params_init and
poly_geometry_params_init zero these pointers, poly_*_params_set_draw does not
touch them, and the setup kernels write them only when the draw fits, so a
dropped draw keeps the sink without PR 77's change to cl/radv_gs_compute.cl.
That kernel cannot read the switch, and leaving it alone keeps an unset switch
identical to before.

This path only runs for geometry shaders with transform feedback, or for every
geometry shader with RADV_PS5_GS_COMPUTE=1.

Not built, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c
index 34840a8..d8af00b 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -14425,6 +14425,9 @@ radv_gs_compute_dispatch(struct radv_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer, const struct radv_s
       RADV_CMD_FLAG_CS_PARTIAL_FLUSH | RADV_CMD_FLAG_INV_VCACHE | RADV_CMD_FLAG_INV_SCACHE;
 }
 
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include "util/u_atomic.h"
+
 /* poly's parameters and the draw block, as far as the CPU knows them. With
  * transform feedback active, returns where the buffers' offsets go for the
  * passes (radv_gs_compute_run_passes), else 0. */
@@ -14440,6 +14443,27 @@ radv_gs_compute_prepare(struct radv_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer, const struct radv_gs
    poly_vertex_params_init(vp, gsc->vs_outputs, wg_size);
    poly_geometry_params_init(gp, mode, wg_size);
 
+   /* EglantinePS5 (from ProsperoEden, by way of heydemoura/EglantinePS5 PR 77): with
+    * RADV_PS5_GS_COMPUTE_SINKS=1 the pointers radv_gs_compute_setup and radv_gs_compute_tess_setup
+    * fill in only for a draw that fits start at a 256-byte sink, not 0. A draw the setup drops
+    * (its counts or the heap do not fit) left them at 0, and the passes that still ran read and
+    * wrote through them: a GPU page fault in a game's battles. poly_*_params_init zero them and
+    * poly_*_params_set_draw does not touch them, so a dropped draw keeps the sink. Read once. */
+   static int sinks = -1;
+   if (unlikely(sinks < 0)) {
+      const char *const value = getenv("RADV_PS5_GS_COMPUTE_SINKS");
+      const int on = value && value[0] == '1' && value[1] == '\0';
+      if (p_atomic_cmpxchg(&sinks, -1, on) == -1 && on)
+         fprintf(stderr, "radv/ps5: dropped geometry-shader compute draws point at a sink (RADV_PS5_GS_COMPUTE_SINKS)\n");
+   }
+   if (sinks) {
+      const uint64_t null_sink = radv_gs_compute_upload(cmd_buffer, 256, NULL, NULL);
+      vp->output_buffer = null_sink;
+      vp->index_buffer = null_sink;
+      gp->count_buffer = null_sink;
+      gp->output_index_buffer = null_sink;
+   }
+
    /* Primitives generated and written per stream count into the command
     * buffer's counters, which queries sample. */
    const uint64_t sink = radv_gs_compute_upload(cmd_buffer, 256, NULL, NULL);
